sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch16-07> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Trabecular arrangement is produced by the forces acting on the bone, not by heredity: when a fracture heals with the parts displaced so that the stress lines are redistributed, the trabecular system is entirely remodelled within weeks to align with the new forces, even at a distance from the injury.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Trabecular architecture remodels to new force patterns after malunited fracture";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XVI, “On Form and Mechanical Efficiency”; topic “Trabecular architecture and stress lines”. Scope: living vertebrate bone after fracture, malunion or transplantation"
}
